WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:11.700
Early the next morning, the computer whirred to life.

2
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:15.115
"Wake up. Time to report to work."

3
00:00:15.116 --> 00:00:20.199
"I'm not going," Ally grumbled, and yanked the covers over her head.

4
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:26.467
"Irrational reply," the computer said. "Need fuel and new parts for travel to Astralia."

5
00:00:26.468 --> 00:00:33.280
"I can't go back to the diner. Mateo hates me," Ally said.

6
00:00:33.281 --> 00:00:40.552
"Irrational reply," the computer repeated. "An Astralian never gives up on a mission."

7
00:00:40.553 --> 00:00:49.649
"Fine!" Ally got up and threw on her meld medallion.

8
00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:52.657
"I'll go find another job! Are you happy?"

9
00:00:52.658 --> 00:00:59.071
"Irrational question," the computer replied.

10
00:00:59.072 --> 00:01:05.561
*** Ally left the park and walked into town to look for a new

11
00:01:05.562 --> 00:01:09.832
job. But in order to get to some of the other businesses, she had to walk past

12
00:01:09.833 --> 00:01:12.086
Ray's. "I'll just run," she

13
00:01:12.087 --> 00:01:18.412
thought. Then, as she got closer to the diner, she spotted Ray and Mateo out

14
00:01:18.413 --> 00:01:21.867
front. She ducked into a nearby

15
00:01:21.868 --> 00:01:26.584
alley. "Mateo, I insist," Ray said. "You must go to camp

16
00:01:26.585 --> 00:01:29.587
today. The last few months have been hard enough on our

17
00:01:29.588 --> 00:01:32.059
family. I want you to have some

18
00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:41.351
fun." "I don't want you to be lonely, Papi. Besides, if Ally has quit, it's all my fault."

19
00:01:41.352 --> 00:01:45.326
"I doubt you're the reason she didn't show up today," Ray said.

20
00:01:45.327 --> 00:01:48.692
"With so few customers, she couldn't make enough money here.

21
00:01:48.693 --> 00:01:52.016
I'm sure she found a better-paying job."

22
00:01:52.017 --> 00:01:56.289
Mateo sighed. "I shouldn't have yelled at her.

23
00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:59.766
Especially since I finally got up the nerve to text Bethany.

24
00:01:59.767 --> 00:02:07.776
Because of Ally, I invited Bethany to the sci-fi convention at the UFO museum next week, and she said yes!"

25
00:02:07.777 --> 00:02:19.368
"That's great, son." Ray wrapped an arm around Mateo's shoulder and led him back inside.

26
00:02:19.369 --> 00:02:21.624
Ally ran a hand through her hair.

27
00:02:21.625 --> 00:02:24.857
"Mateo's not mad at me anymore," she thought.

28
00:02:24.858 --> 00:02:29.545
"And Ray needs my help. Maybe . . ."

29
00:02:29.546 --> 00:02:35.472
A minute later she strolled into the diner as if nothing had ever happened. "I'm sorry I'm late, I—"

30
00:02:35.473 --> 00:02:38.612
"You're back," Ray said.

31
00:02:38.613 --> 00:02:42.584
"I'm sorry I yelled at you, Ally," Mateo said.

32
00:02:42.585 --> 00:02:45.932
"I was just embarrassed in front of Bethany."

33
00:02:45.933 --> 00:02:50.377
Ally waved her hand. "I've already forgotten about it.

34
00:02:50.378 --> 00:02:53.391
Don't you have a camp to get to, Mateo?"

35
00:02:53.392 --> 00:03:09.688
"Yes," he said. "And thanks to you, I've also got a date with Bethany!"

36
00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:13.330
*** Later in the day, customers began to trickle

37
00:03:13.331 --> 00:03:20.112
in. There was a family of four who ordered burgers, fries, and

38
00:03:20.113 --> 00:03:26.282
milkshakes. There was also a woman with bright red hair, rhinestone glasses, and a leopard-print

39
00:03:26.283 --> 00:03:30.268
dress. Phil came running

40
00:03:30.269 --> 00:03:33.744
in. "Just a coffee to go. I've got to get back to the

41
00:03:33.745 --> 00:03:37.942
museum. There's a big alien-hunting crowd over there

42
00:03:37.943 --> 00:03:41.407
today." "What?" Ally's stomach turned to

43
00:03:41.408 --> 00:03:47.383
knots. She tried to read Phil's mind, but all she could see was a

44
00:03:47.384 --> 00:03:50.367
doughnut. "You know, a huge tour group," Phil

45
00:03:50.368 --> 00:03:58.008
said. "They come to the museum thinking they'll find proof of aliens and UFOs and try to track them down. Can you

46
00:03:58.009 --> 00:04:06.203
imagine?" Ally gave a little laugh. "Nope!" Then she handed Phil his coffee and a

47
00:04:06.204 --> 00:04:09.535
doughnut. "Here, it's on the

48
00:04:09.536 --> 00:04:15.052
house." "Chocolate! My favorite. How'd you know?" Phil

49
00:04:15.053 --> 00:04:22.934
asked. She shrugged. "Lucky

50
00:04:22.935 --> 00:04:29.157
guess." Ally put some of her tip money in the cash register to pay for Phil's

51
00:04:29.158 --> 00:04:32.989
doughnut. Then she went to serve the woman in the leopard-print

52
00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:35.158
dress. "Do you know what you'd

53
00:04:35.159 --> 00:04:39.348
like?" "I wish I did." The woman stared at the

54
00:04:39.349 --> 00:04:41.833
menu. "Let's see if I can help," Ally said.

55
00:04:41.834 --> 00:04:48.253
She quickly scanned the woman's thoughts and saw a plate of eggs with spicy salsa.

56
00:04:48.254 --> 00:04:51.672
"How about Ray's huevos rancheros?

57
00:04:51.673 --> 00:04:56.734
That's two fried eggs on a crispy tortilla, salsa, and cheese."

58
00:04:56.735 --> 00:04:58.824
The woman's face lit up.

59
00:04:58.825 --> 00:05:02.069
"That's exactly what I've been craving.

60
00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:11.757
I didn't see it on the menu, but you read my mind!"

61
00:05:11.758 --> 00:05:17.347
Ten minutes later Ally was crossing the dining room with the woman's order and trying not to think about what Phil had said.

62
00:05:17.348 --> 00:05:21.102
It sounded like some humans actually hunted for aliens.

63
00:05:21.103 --> 00:05:24.679
"I'm in more danger than I realized," Ally thought.

64
00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:28.513
She hadn't been looking where she was going. "Maybe I'd better—oops!"

65
00:05:28.514 --> 00:05:32.417
As Ally slammed into an empty table, the plate of eggs flew up into the air.

66
00:05:32.418 --> 00:05:35.547
Instinctively Ally activated her levitating ability.

67
00:05:35.548 --> 00:05:38.177
The plate froze, floating in midair.

68
00:05:38.178 --> 00:05:41.756
"Ack!" she thought. "I shouldn't have done that!"

69
00:05:41.757 --> 00:05:46.138
Ally quickly grabbed the plate and looked around to see if anyone had spotted her trick.

70
00:05:46.139 --> 00:05:49.463
The woman in the leopard-print dress was looking right at her.

71
00:05:49.464 --> 00:05:55.782
When Ally met her eyes, the woman quickly looked away.

